        "original_id": "8b0107e3-7cef-589a-9417-87772241e4bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Corylopsis, Impatiens\n- Taxonomy: genera, species counts, Hamamelidaceae\n- Places: eastern Asia, China, Japan, Korea, the Himalayas, Northern Hemisphere, tropics\n\nFacts:\n- Corylopsis is a genus of nearly 30 species of shrubs in the witch hazel family, Hamamelidaceae.\n- Corylopsis is native to eastern Asia, and most Corylopsis species are endemic to China, with some also found in Japan, Korea, and the Himalayas.\n- Impatiens is a genus of about 850 to 1,000 species of flowering plants.\n- Impatiens is widely distributed throughout the Northern Hemisphere and the tropics.",
